      "writtenOn": "2026-09-30T18:19:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not really sure that we do need to make this distinction: what do know is that the operation did not succeed and therefore we *must* tell the caller.\n\nThere could be two conditions because the operation did not succeed:\n\n1. The CAS failed *because of the interruption came before* the operation could complete\n2. The CAS failed *regardless* of the interruption, because instead another concurrent operation took over and won the race.\n\nThe question is: what should the client do differently in case 1. or 2.?\n\nIMHO both cases are the same case: the operation did not succeed and we should return `false` in both situations.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 216,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 227,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "948794a800961e3cea10af5050ed65311a1d1c3f",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
